<body>

<!-- ===== HEADER ===== -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header-tag">Energy Market Intelligence · Trend Analysis</div>
    <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends:<br><span>A Historical Analysis (1970–2026)</span></h1>
    <div class="header-meta">
      <span><strong>Coverage:</strong> Jan 1970 – Mar 2026</span>
      <span><strong>Observations:</strong> {len(df):,} monthly data points</span>
      <span><strong>Metric:</strong> USD/bbl (nominal)</span>
      <span><strong>Source:</strong> Kaggle / Global Fuel Price Trends Dataset</span>
      <span><strong>Generated:</strong> April 2026</span>
    </div>
    <nav class="toc" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <a href="#exec-overview">Executive Overview</a>
      <a href="#long-term">Long-Term Trajectory</a>
      <a href="#decade">Decade Breakdown</a>
      <a href="#volatility">Volatility & Shocks</a>
      <a href="#statistical">Statistical Summary</a>
      <a href="#outlook">Outlook & Conclusions</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW ===== -->
<div class="section" id="exec-overview">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-id">01 · Executive Overview</div>
      <h2>Five Decades of Crude Oil: From $1.21 to $132.83</h2>
      <p>A high-level synthesis of the dataset scope, primary price trajectory, and critical analytical findings. All figures are in nominal USD/bbl derived directly from 675 monthly observations spanning January 1970 through March 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- KPI Row -->
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--accent);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Price Range (All-Time)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value kpi-accent">${price_range:.2f}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">${overall_min:.2f} ({min_date}) → ${overall_max:.2f} ({max_date})</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--accent2);">
        <div class="kpi-label">CAGR (1970–2026)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--accent2);">{cagr:.2f}%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">$1.21 → ${last_price:.2f} over {n_years:.1f} years</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--red);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Max Monthly Change</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--red);">+{max_mom_pct:.0f}%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">{max_mom_pct_date} — OPEC Oil Embargo aftermath</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--purple);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Highest-Avg Decade</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--purple);">{dec_labels[decade_highest]}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Avg ${decade_stats.loc[decade_highest,'avg']:.2f}/bbl</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--green);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Price Volatility (σ)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--green);">${overall_std:.2f}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Standard deviation across all 675 monthly observations</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Structural Narrative:</strong> Crude oil prices have undergone three distinct structural regimes over 56 years. The pre-1973 era was characterized by near-flat prices below $2/bbl, controlled largely by the major Western oil companies. The 1973 OPEC embargo marked a permanent step-change, with prices entering a volatile $10–$40 range through the 1980s and 1990s. The 2000s inaugurated a supercycle driven by Chinese industrialization and financial speculation, peaking at $132.83 in July 2008 before the global financial crisis caused the sharpest absolute price collapse on record. Post-GFC recovery created the 2010–2014 plateau near $100/bbl, followed by the 2014–2016 shale-era price war, the COVID-19 demand shock in 2020, and a rapid recovery driven by geopolitical disruption in 2022.
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box blue">
      <strong>Dataset Note:</strong> All 675 observations are present with no null values. The dataset covers January 1970 through March 2026 at monthly granularity. Prices are in nominal USD; no inflation adjustment is applied. Data points from late 2025 onward may include projected or estimated values per the dataset documentation.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: LONG-TERM TRAJECTORY ===== -->
