<!-- ===== SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW ===== -->
<div class="section" id="exec-overview">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-id">01 · Executive Overview</div>
      <h2>Five Decades of Crude Oil: From $1.21 to $132.83</h2>
      <p>A high-level synthesis of the dataset scope, primary price trajectory, and critical analytical findings. All figures are in nominal USD/bbl derived directly from 675 monthly observations spanning January 1970 through March 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- KPI Row -->
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--accent);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Price Range (All-Time)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value kpi-accent">${price_range:.2f}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">${overall_min:.2f} ({min_date}) → ${overall_max:.2f} ({max_date})</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--accent2);">
        <div class="kpi-label">CAGR (1970–2026)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--accent2);">{cagr:.2f}%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">$1.21 → ${last_price:.2f} over {n_years:.1f} years</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--red);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Max Monthly Change</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--red);">+{max_mom_pct:.0f}%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">{max_mom_pct_date} — OPEC Oil Embargo aftermath</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--purple);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Highest-Avg Decade</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--purple);">{dec_labels[decade_highest]}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Avg ${decade_stats.loc[decade_highest,'avg']:.2f}/bbl</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color: var(--green);">
        <div class="kpi-label">Price Volatility (σ)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--green);">${overall_std:.2f}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Standard deviation across all 675 monthly observations</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Structural Narrative:</strong> Crude oil prices have undergone three distinct structural regimes over 56 years. The pre-1973 era was characterized by near-flat prices below $2/bbl, controlled largely by the major Western oil companies. The 1973 OPEC embargo marked a permanent step-change, with prices entering a volatile $10–$40 range through the 1980s and 1990s. The 2000s inaugurated a supercycle driven by Chinese industrialization and financial speculation, peaking at $132.83 in July 2008 before the global financial crisis caused the sharpest absolute price collapse on record. Post-GFC recovery created the 2010–2014 plateau near $100/bbl, followed by the 2014–2016 shale-era price war, the COVID-19 demand shock in 2020, and a rapid recovery driven by geopolitical disruption in 2022.
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box blue">
      <strong>Dataset Note:</strong> All 675 observations are present with no null values. The dataset covers January 1970 through March 2026 at monthly granularity. Prices are in nominal USD; no inflation adjustment is applied. Data points from late 2025 onward may include projected or estimated values per the dataset documentation.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: LONG-TERM TRAJECTORY ===== -->
<div class="section" id="long-term">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-id">02 · Long-Term Price Trajectory</div>
      <h2>Monthly Crude Oil Prices, January 1970 – March 2026</h2>
      <p>Full time-series visualization of 675 monthly observations. Key inflection points are annotated. The chart renders the complete trajectory from the pre-embargo era through the 2026 data.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Monthly Spot Price — Crude Oil (USD/bbl)</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">675 monthly observations · Nominal USD · Source: Global Fuel Price Trends Dataset</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:420px;">
        <canvas id="chartLongTerm"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="annotation-labels" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">A</span> 1973 Oil Embargo</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">B</span> 1979 Iranian Revolution</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">C</span> 1986 OPEC Price Collapse</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">D</span> 1990 Gulf War</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">E</span> 1998 Asian Crisis Low</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">F</span> 2008 Financial Crisis Peak</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">G</span> 2014 Shale Glut Collapse</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">H</span> 2020 COVID-19 Crash</div>
        <div class="ann-label"><span style="color:#f0a500;">I</span> 2022 Russia-Ukraine War</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-card" style="margin-top:0;">
      <div class="chart-title">Annual Average Price (USD/bbl)</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">Year-level aggregation of monthly averages — smooths intra-year volatility</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:280px;">
        <canvas id="chartAnnual"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="insight-box">
        <strong>Pre-1973 Era:</strong> Prices were extraordinarily stable at $1.21/bbl through all of 1970. Gradual escalation to ~$2.08/bbl by early 1973 reflected modest OPEC price adjustments but no structural volatility.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box">
        <strong>1973–74 Shock:</strong> The OPEC embargo triggered the most extreme single-month percentage gain in the dataset: +217% in January 1974 ($4.10 → $13.00). This single event permanently reset the global energy price floor.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box blue">
        <strong>2000s Supercycle:</strong> Prices rose from ~$25 in 2000 to $132.83 in July 2008—a 5.3× increase in 8 years. This was driven by Chinese demand growth, financial speculation, and limited spare OPEC capacity. The GFC erased 68% of value in 5 months.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box blue">
        <strong>Post-2014 Structural Shift:</strong> The shale revolution created persistent oversupply. Prices have not returned to the 2011–2014 $100+ plateau. The 2020s range ($60–$120) reflects this structural reset, plus OPEC+ supply management.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 3: DECADE BY DECADE ===== -->
<div class="section" id="decade">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-id">03 · Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</div>
      <h2>Structural Shifts Across Six Decades</h2>
      <p>Comparing average prices, volatility, and defining characteristics across each decade reveals how the fundamental pricing environment has evolved from OPEC-controlled stability to complex multi-factor dynamics.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Average Price by Decade</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Mean monthly price (USD/bbl) per decade</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:260px;">
          <canvas id="chartDecadeAvg"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Price Volatility by Decade (σ)</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Standard deviation of monthly prices per decade</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:260px;">
          <canvas id="chartDecadeStd"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Decade Price Range: Min / Avg / Max</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">Full price dispersion within each decade</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:300px;">
        <canvas id="chartDecadeRange"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="overflow-x:auto; margin-bottom:24px;">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Decade</th>
            <th>Avg Price</th>
            <th>Std Dev (σ)</th>
            <th>Min Price</th>
            <th>Max Price</th>
            <th>Observations</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {decade_table_rows}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="three-col">
      <div class="insight-box">
        <strong>1970s:</strong> Average $9.70/bbl but σ=$8.89—near-100% coefficient of variation. The decade was defined by two oil shocks (1973 embargo, 1979 Iranian Revolution) that transformed energy markets permanently.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box">
        <strong>1980s–90s:</strong> The 1986 OPEC quota collapse crashed prices to ~$9.62/bbl. The 1990s were the most price-stable decade post-embargo, with σ=$3.84 and a range of just $24/bbl, despite the Gulf War spike.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box blue">
        <strong>2000s:</strong> The highest-volatility decade (σ=$25.64) despite having the second-highest average. Extreme range from $18.52 (post-9/11) to $132.83 (Jul 2008). China's rise + financial speculation amplified moves.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box blue">
        <strong>2010s:</strong> The highest-average decade at $76.45/bbl. The 2011–2014 period maintained near-$100 prices before the 2014 shale glut caused a 65% drawdown by early 2016. Significant structural turning point.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box green">
        <strong>2020s (partial):</strong> Only 75 months of data. COVID-19 caused the lowest price since 1999 ($21.04 in April 2020). Subsequent recovery to $116.80 and gradual normalization to the $60–$90 range define this era.
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box red">
        <strong>Key Insight:</strong> The 1990s was the only post-OPEC decade where prices trended <em>lower</em> than the preceding decade. Every other inter-decade transition saw higher average prices, confirming a long-run structural uptrend.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 4: VOLATILITY & SHOCKS ===== -->
<div class="section" id="volatility">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-id">04 · Price Volatility & Major Shocks</div>
      <h2>Quantifying Extreme Price Events</h2>
      <p>Precise measurement of month-over-month percentage changes identifies the sharpest price dislocations in the dataset. Rolling 12-month standard deviation maps volatility regimes over time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-card">
